  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\n**Research consolidation (credit and provenance). No new \u03ba, construction, ledger or disposition change.**\n\nMain retains open PR #1015's work verbatim, but no ledger row, CONTRIBUTORS entry or retained notice records it. This corrects an omission in my own merged #1062, which copied the file.\n\n- `research/r439-bsection-stars-seed01/inputs/PR1015-CANDIDATE.json`, merged with #1062, has git blob `16532f2d`. That is identical to `research/r439-bsection-multwrite/CANDIDATE.json` at #1015's open head `7588c797`.\n- Its nine phase-B block programs supply **244 of #1062's 283 saved ADDs** (11,783 \u2192 11,500). #923's frame 520 supplies 24 and the rerun star pass 15, recomputed from #1062's `CERTIFICATE.json`.\n- Gaps at base:\n  - `pr-ledger.json` has a #1062 row whose scope names \"nine PR1015 blocks\", and no #1015 row;\n  - `CONTRIBUTORS.md` has no #1015 entry;\n  - #1015's `NOTICE.md` (Apache-2.0 offer, AI disclosure \"Prepared with help from opencode\", predecessor credits) was not retained beside the copied file. #1062's README and SOURCES.json do credit and pin #1015.\n\nThe change has two parts:\n\n- `research/r439-pr1015-retention-seed95/` contains `RECEIPT.json`, `README.md`, `verify.py` and `NOTICE-PR1015.md`. The last is #1015's NOTICE byte for byte (blob `727d5b58`).\n- `CONTRIBUTORS.md` gets one line in the batch #1099 section crediting Aaron Wang / navinor for #1015, following the #946 \"credited as pending integration\" precedent.\n\nLedger and disposition updates are left to maintainers, and #1015 stays open for its own review. \u03ba is unaffected: the selected #1094 uses the PR589 bit word, and the bit side does not bind.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\n- Task card: consolidation track, `overlap-receipt` (scope key `5ae821d1b52092164092`), from `scripts/choose_research_task.py --track consolidation`. The track came from OS-random seed 95 under the user's sprint assignment.\n- Base: `1b59b624` (prepared on `c0e3631d`; CONTRIBUTORS, the ledger and the #1062 package are unchanged between the two).\n- Heads observed on 2026-10-14: #1015 `7588c797`, #1122 `a2551e70`, #1127 `2e9dc9d3`.\n- Overlap checked against open PRs through #1168, the ledger, batch-1099 records and discussions #1163/#1166/#1167. No receipt or credit fix for #1015 exists.\n- #1122 and #1127 are constructions, not receipts. The README adds two read-only reviewer notes:\n  - #1122 is a strict superset of merged #1062 plus #980's A part, and its \"pending PR1062\" wording is stale;\n  - #1127's moves all overlap the regions #1062 and #980 already rewrite, so they are not additive as packaged.\n- Five explorer subagents evaluated alternative consolidation scopes and three judges scored them; this credit gap is the new, hash-checkable part.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/r439-pr1015-retention-seed95/verify.py\n```\n\nExpected (read-only, no network, standard library only):\n\n```text\nbase ledger: #1015 row absent (gap recorded)\nPASS_R439_PR1015_RETENTION blob=16532f2d saving=PR1015:244+PR923:24+star15=283 controls=2\n```\n\n- The script recomputes both git blob ids, the per-source saving split, and the presence of the credit line.\n- The missing ledger row is asserted only while the ledger is still the base blob; after a maintainer update the script reports the new state instead of failing.\n- Two negative controls must fail: a block misattributed to PR923, and a one-byte change to the retained file.\n- Not run: the reviewer notes on #1122 and #1127 come from their packages at the stated heads and are not checked by the script. No native replay is needed, because no artifact changes.\n\n## Credit\n\n- Aaron Wang / navinor for #1015's block programs and notice.\n- Ross Richardson for #923's frame-520 program.\n- #967 (prepared for @theon199) and the #926/#915 helper-star lineage.\n- Gareth Davidson for #1122.\n- #1127's authors.\n\n`NOTICE-PR1015.md` is retained under Apache-2.0. Prepared by Sagar Thakrar with substantial assistance from Anthropic Claude (Claude Code), including the explorer and judge subagents.\n",
